# tenant-vocabulary.baseline — the ratchet on tenant words above their
# tier, read by infra/lint/no-tenant-vocabulary-above-its-tier.sh
# (backlog be39298f). One line per tier: `<tier> <count>`.
#
# Each number is the lint's OWN measurement of the tree on the day it
# was written, and it only goes down: the lint refuses a tier whose
# count is above its line (the leak grew) and a tier whose count is
# below it (lower the line in the same car). Nobody raises one. The
# target is zero in every tier, held there by the same refusal.
#
# Written 2026-09-16 from the lint's measurement of origin/main b4d7a0fd
# plus this car — the brewery's and the used-device shop's VOCABULARY
# together, 23 terms, with a tenant's name as a path or an id exempt.
crates/core 375
crates/modules 445
crates/orchestrators 836
apps/web/src 310
apps/simulator 55
infra/postgres/schema 202
infra/platform 2
infra/cluster 8
